Hi Rory,

Just so that I understand, what would the biology be that would create sigma~Bk. I’ve only ever used Bk on g0 as I envision it acting on the height of the detection function not necessarily the spatial extent (sigma).

I would personally be ok using the g0~Bk and sigma~1. Unless there is a really good biological reason that sigma also needs Bk. Which there very well may be.

Also, are al your spatial habitat covariates standardized? I’ve had most convergence issues when not standardized. But that’s not always the solution to convergence issues either.

Cheers,
Clayton

