Looking more closely at the old emails included in this email chain... Are the sigma estimates at the bottom in meters? If so, this is 32 km for 2012 and 16 km for 2016, which are substantially larger than any reported sigmas I've seen. Are these consistent with expected leopard home range sizes?

The state space may already be so large that increasing it even further may not noticeably change the parameter estimates, so that might not be a good test for a sigma that is not identifiable. If the sigmas are very inconsistent with expected space use, it is very likely because sigma is not identifiable in this data set.

Ben

