Hey Murray,

Thanks so much for the prompt response. I am using an older version (3.2.1). I will update.

after a couple errors I was able to specify all model parameters. To hopefully help others with the same issue, I provided my code and a brief explanation.

Thanks again for your help!

I am running a multi-session model. For simplicity, this example shows specifics for one site.

### make read.capthist()

> Capthist_Site1<- read.capthist("Site1_Capture.txt", "Site1_Trap_wcov.txt", detector = "multi", trapcovnames = 'Cover')

Note: "Cover" is a detector specific, user defined, covariate added in the read.capthist step (above). Cover classes are 0,1,2,3.

### combine all sites:

> Capthist_All_Sites<-MS.capthist(Capthist_Site1,Capthist_Site2, ... Capthist_Site13)

### make.mask()

> Mask_Site1 <- make.mask(traps(Site1), buffer=400,spacing = 25, type='trapbuffer')

### combine all masks:

> Mask_All_Sites <- list(Mask_Site1, Mask_Site2, … Mask_Site13)

### load sessioncov file ###

> session_cov<-read.csv("session_cov.csv")

> session_cov
   session       act
1   Site1     0.4118559
2   Site2     0.3876989
.....................
13  Site13    0.7081735

Final model:

> fit<-secr.fit(capthist = Capthist_All_Sites, mask = Mask_All_Sites, sessioncov = session_cov, model = list(D ~ session, g0 ~ k + Cover, sigma ~ act), detectfn = "EX")

Note: "act" is a session specific, user defined, covariate where each site (n=13) has a session specific value.

